  "actualRepair": [
    "One existing producer owner now creates exactly one ephemeral RSA2048/SHA256 self-signed Code Signing identity, the documented owned-testing form in Apple TN2206. It is the sole generation path, not a fallback after any failure.",
    "The helper writes a fixed 277-byte public request configuration in the already-owned temporary directory and selects its exact extension section. It does not inherit host v3_ca defaults or add duplicate critical OIDs; no real/user certificate shape or policy changes.",
    "The same actual certificate bytes are the leaf and explicit code/profile test anchor. The same private key signs actual codesign output and both real embedded profile CMS layers; all profiles still name SHA256 of that actual code certificate. Original prefixes, teams, application identifiers, resource seals and entitlements are unchanged.",
    "PKCS12 includes this one certificate and its matching private key in memory; no duplicate certfile bag. Existing stdin privacy, same owned Keychain importer/C bridge, fresh unlock/search/challenge, actual codesign command and exact detached CodeDirectory CMS checks remain required.",
    "Original platform main/extensions/framework compile/sign, profile/DER, exact raw CMS checks and output/archive tail are byte-identical. No alternate signing backend, ad-hoc signature, global trust/search list, source-only bypass, missing-fixture skip or private-key file is added."
  ],
  "hypothesisAndCoverage": {
    "supportedChoice": "A self-signed identity is publicly documented for testing signing machinery and needs no separate issuer certificate lookup. The prior CA-issued identity required a separate issuer; current codesign identity selection and later chain construction are not equivalent to raw key-use enumeration or an explicit-anchor trust call.",
    "notProven": "The exact deployed codesign filtering/chain/ACL cause of the prior item-not-found remains unproved. A self-signed form may still be rejected by the actual next platform run.",
    "preservedCoverage": "Existing independent owned CA+leaf fixtures, generic anchor-chain verification, production Apple authorization limitations and strict verifier algorithms are unchanged. The same-job platform fixture alone changes to a one-certificate explicit-anchor shape.",
    "chainContract": "Generic CMS permits a nonempty verified leaf-to-explicit-anchor chain of length1..16; it checks actual SecKey signature, date, networkfalse and exact last anchor. The loader passes its one real anchor to both code/profile verification. No production trust-policy change is needed to represent a length1 owned chain.",
    "gateInputs": "SDK producer remains7 existing sources; finite runner remains19 inputs. Only existing generator and portable test bytes change. Root owns the next immutable tag/full-currentcore binding; this delta changes no selection identity, budget, native test or artifact allowlist."
  },
